WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
Translation: Ishin-Digital

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.960
The final summer vacation of middle school ended.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.490
A new semester has begun.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:49.210
We started using reference books during the vacation.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.210
Everyone is more attentive during class.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.520
Everyone is thinking about the entrance exam.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.780
Hey, Nozomu-kun!

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.820
We made these.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.670
We want you to wear them.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.010
I will, thank you.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.910
We’re so glad!

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.330
I’m happy, but is it okay?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.180
Since that day,

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.670
Kira-chan and Yura-chan’s attitudes have changed.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.420
Incredible, Nozomu!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.400
Er, yeah…

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:42.510
You’re thinking about entering the same high school as the Sakurazuki sisters?

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.440
It’s not that!

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.890
It’s no lie!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.430
But in reality…

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.100
The only school offering aeronautics…

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.670
I can’t lose to this guy!

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.540
Hey!

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.090
It’s raining…

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.910
Nozomu-kun!

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.360
So, you don’t have an umbrella?

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.690
No, I don’t.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.330
Use this, then!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.170
But…

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.940
We’re fine.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:20.010
See you tomorrow, Nozomu-kun!

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.270
Nozomu-kun, I forgot my umbrella.
May I share yours?

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:26.980
Keisuke!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.850
Traitor.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.590
There’s definitely something going on between you and the Sakurazuki sisters.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.020
Are you sure?

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.400
Of course!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.800
Maybe you’re going out with the Sakurazuki sisters?

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.030
Are you going out with them?

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.160
What!

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.730
No! There’s no way…

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.120
Just kidding! We just wanted to say that, for once.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.300
See you later!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.330
Ah, the Ichijou sisters
are also so very cute!

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.200
If Nozomu has his sights set on the Sakurazuki sisters,

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.840
it’ll be okay if I go after
the Ichijou sisters!

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.930
We’re okay.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.730
Well, see you tomorrow, Nozomu-kun!

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.800
Maybe you’re going out with the Sakurazuki sisters?

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.250
Are you going out with them?

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.810
So, who should I…

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.040
Huh?

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.760
Who is that?
It’s the first time I’ve seen her…

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.290
Eh?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.790
I’m sorry.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:02.440
Eh?

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.950
That drawing… It’s mine.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:10.240
Ah… umm… here you go.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.580
Thank you for picking them up for me.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.170
It’s not a problem. They’re sketches of the Soujin Temple, right?

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:24.670
It’s a bit embarrassing. I don’t draw well.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.930
That’s not true! You do draw very well. Honest!

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.810
Really?

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:34.680
Really. I was quite surprised.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.750
Even though I don’t understand drawing very well,

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.370
in my opinion,
your drawings were great.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.740
They were really great!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:48.120
Thank you. This is the first time someone has complimented me this way.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.930
Therefore, I’m really happy.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.460
Are you okay?

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.960
It turned cold suddenly.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.180
Yeah.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.210
I have to go home now.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.300
Okay.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.360
Goodbye.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.590
Umm… is it okay to come again?

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.430
Of course.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.160
Bye.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:22.920
It’s already October…

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:29.240
So what are we gonna do, Nozomu?

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.180
Hey, Nozomu!

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.160
What?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.710
Don’t give me a “What?”

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.500
I’m asking what we should do
for the cultural festival.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.740
Oh yeah.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:45.980
I think that a “scary café” would be very interesting.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:47.670
What do you think?

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.070
It’s a good idea.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.880
This cultural festival is a good chance!

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:57.200
Lots of girls from the neighboring girls’ schools will be coming.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:58.560
I’m all fired up!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.100
Not again…

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:03.250
I always research my stuff thoroughly.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.640
Even though I’m really thinking about the Sakurazuki sisters…

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.990
Ah, so you’re here!

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.310
Have you finished your meal?

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.780
We would like you to eat the dessert that we’ve brought.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.120
Wow, apple pie!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.250
Previously, it didn’t come out right, remember?

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.070
So we practiced many times.

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:24.980
We finally got it to turn out right… after 52 tries.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:27.530
It was actually 53 times, Kira-chan.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.170
Oh, is that so?

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:33.960
The taste is all right this time. We’ve tried it.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.340
So please taste it, Nozomu-kun.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.430
Ah, you’re welcome to try as well, Kosaka-kun.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.940
Is that okay? You didn’t intend for you three to eat it?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:46.210
No, it’s okay. We ate before we came here.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.440
Right?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.110
Please eat!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.550
Okay, I’ll dig in!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.490
It’s good!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.170
We’re so happy!

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:57.650
You too, Nozomu-kun!

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:58.890
O-Okay…

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.010
Speaking of which,

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:03.410
what do you think the theme for our cultural festival booth should be?

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:05.540
It’s our first time,

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.900
so we don’t quite understand.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.370
Ah, is that so?

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.770
But, it looks like it’s going to be really interesting!

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.290
We’re looking forward to it.
Right, Kira-chan?

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.050
I see.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.850
Okay, I’m even more fired up now!

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.200
We’ll go on ahead.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.750
Um… wait.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.080
Ah… thank you for the apple pie.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.290
That’s okay.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:29.400
You made the apple pie for me… and lent me your umbrella the other time…

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:35.710
Is that okay? At this rate…

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.480
It’s okay. Don’t worry.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:42.050
It’s a pleasure. Right, Kira-chan?

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.290
Yeah. It’s a pleasure, Yura-chan.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.720
So don’t worry about it.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:49.380
See you later!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.930
This is so good!

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.710
I think you’ve eaten too much.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:54.550
Huh?

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.680
Am I good enough for them?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:06.300
He had no idea what that was,
so he accepted the task alone!

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:06.940
Hahaha!

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.410
He’s a really funny guy!

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.190
Yeah, yeah…

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:11.070
And then everyone was cracking up…

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.340
Hey, there!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:37.300
Ah… when you came yesterday, I…

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.890
That’s all right. I was wondering whether you would come.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.240
Really?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.250
Yeah.

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.820
This one’s from some time ago, right?

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.320
Yeah.

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.890
I don’t draw very well.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:00.310
No, no. You drew this really…

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.960
Umm… that’s…

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.720
Oh yeah… I know of a great place.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.720
I’ll take you there.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.030
Eh?

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:42.970
Are you doing okay?
It’s just a little further.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:44.910
Okay.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:48.910
Come.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:17.450
The same scenery becomes boring after a while.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:19.890
This place is pretty good, right?

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:24.020
Yes. I never knew there was such a place.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.950
If I had known sooner…

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:27.090
Eh?

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:29.960
It’s nothing.

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:32.750
“Soujyu”?

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.960
Yes. It’s the “soujyu” in “sarasoujyu”.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.290
I’m Shirogane Soujyu.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.950
I’m Futami Nozomu.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.840
You’re in the Souai middle school,
third year.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:45.400
I can tell by your uniform
and your badge.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:46.900
I see.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:51.840
Umm… may I call you “Soujyu-chan”?

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:52.670
Of course.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:53.840
How about you, Soujyu-chan?

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.820
I’m in middle school, first year.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.070
First year?

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:01.880
But I don’t go to school often.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.680
I’ve never really been in good health since I was young.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.070
I took a lot of days off.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:10.510
Oh no… was it bad to drag you over here?

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:13.120
No, it isn’t.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.310
I’m glad you brought me here. Really.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:19.840
I’m really happy that I can come here.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:21.590
Yeah.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:27.980
I don’t have many friends, so I often draw alone and so on…

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:28.930
Is that so?

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.160
This was the first time.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:30.600
Eh?

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.470
This was the first time that someone praised my drawing.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.360
Hence, I’m really happy.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:40.820
That was just an offhand remark,
and yet it made her this happy.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:43.660
It’s done!

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.840
It’s really good!

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.140
Thank you.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.230
It’s Onii-chan!

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.250
It’s the drawing-oneechan!

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.600
Did you come here to draw again?

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.310
Let us see!

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:05.010
You two know her?

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.430
Yeah, we ran into her before!

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:11.130
She draws over there, and she draws very well!

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:12.230
Right?

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:17.000
About a week ago, I was around the grave of the twins.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.690
Billy!

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.740
Billy is good friends with her!

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:30.160
That little rascal does that every time he sees a cute girl…

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.470
It’s incredible!

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:32.660
Really!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:36.870
Hey Onee-chan, can you draw us?

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:37.790
Eh?

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.880
Draw us with Billy and Onii-chan!

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:41.970
Okay…

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:46.630
Don’t force her. She prefers landscape drawing.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.700
I’ll try to draw it.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:50.580
Eh?

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:54.730
Yippee! Please do so!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.470
Is it okay?

00:13:57.470 --> 00:14:01.020
Yes, I would like to
leave behind memories…

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.020
Eh?

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:03.760
Final memories…

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:07.220
Well, how is this?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.910
Draw us as pretty as possible!

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.240
Okay!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.170
Onii-san, I’ll draw you separately.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:17.710
Okay.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.250
“Final memories…”

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:31.890
So then, everyone decides by themselves what to dress as… is that fine?

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.570
Okay!

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:37.340
Then, shall we say… any sort of monster or ghost?

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:40.410
Anything we want? Sounds interesting!

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:41.570
WE AGREE!

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:44.940
Why do I have to go buy things?

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.390
What’s wrong with that?
Just accompany me.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.050
But today…

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:49.910
There they are!

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.870
Hey, have you decided on your booth’s theme for the cultural festival?

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:57.330
Ours is a “scary café” – it was my idea.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.870
Eh?

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.720
How about your class?

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.350
Our class will do a “magic café”.

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:03.880
Magic? What’s that?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.510
You’ll see at the cultural festival.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:11.080
We’re going out to buy some stuff.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.350
What a coincidence! We’re going too.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:14.850
Really?

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:17.340
Let’s go, okay? Okay?

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:18.330
Okay!

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:22.070
So, what will you be dressing up as, Nozomu-chan?

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.310
I have no idea.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.650
That’s a lot of differently colored paper.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.160
Isn’t this one good?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.570
This one is pretty!

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.040
How is this?

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:42.670
Why, you…

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:49.330
Onee-chan…

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.660
How is it?

00:15:57.770 --> 00:16:01.350
I was almost certain… Nah, I’m paranoid.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.930
Onii-chan!

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:03.980
You’re late!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:06.490
Sorry for coming back late.

00:16:07.890 --> 00:16:09.280
Welcome back.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.780
Compared to yesterday, it’s mostly done.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:14.410
Yes.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.660
We want to see!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.740
We want to see! We want to see!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.000
No, you’ll have to wait till the drawing is done.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.750
Stingy!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:25.090
If you keep those strange expressions, I’ll draw you like that.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.370
And that’s it for today.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.050
Please, come with us!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:41.300
We don’t understand…

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.440
where the store is, or what to buy.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.040
All right, I’ll…

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:48.880
Thank you!

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:49.830
So, let’s hurry!

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:50.690
Let’s go!

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.060
Wow!

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:55.700
Amazing!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.620
Eh, there are so many here…

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.000
Nozomu-kun, how is this?

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.670
It’s good?

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:14.450
As a matter of fact, this is Papa’s trial #99.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:17.010
“Try to do a cosplay.”

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.050
Eh?

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.800
Oh, we’re just kidding.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:20.390
Just kidding!

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.700
That’s really interesting.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:24.570
Sure.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:26.600
Hey, Nozomu-kun, please look!

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.480
So, what did you decide to get?

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.480
We’ll show you soon.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.100
You’ll definitely be surprised!

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:36.780
Right?

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.160
Okay, we’re going.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.360
See you later! Thanks for today.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.450
See you tomorrow!

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:44.320
Okay.

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.550
Ui-san! Koi-san!

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.000
Okay, I’m done drawing!

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.230
Wow!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.380
I worked on it a little last night.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.570
It looks real!

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.070
Billy looks so cute!

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:20.220
I’m glad.

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:23.680
I wanted to show this to
Nozomu-oniichan. He’s late.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:25.870
You were going to draw him today…

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.000
Yeah, let me go look around.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.850
We’re going to show this to Mom!

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:31.830
Okay.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.490
Soujyu! Are you okay?

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.650
Sara-chan? Why are you here?

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:54.460
I thought I told you not to push yourself!

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:56.960
You’ve already caught a bit of a cold! Are you okay?

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:00.320
We need to hurry home. Can you stand?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.120
Yes.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.530
But, I still have to draw Onii-san…

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:07.370
Right now, getting home and resting is more important!

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:22.220
Onii-san is definitely very kind… just like I thought.

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:23.620
Yeah.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.000
Really!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.710
If only you met Onii-san, you would definitely…

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:31.520
Don’t say too much. Rest well.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:44.530
Soujyu-chan didn’t come yesterday or the day before. I wonder why she stopped coming.

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:46.100
Hey!

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:48.990
Good morning. You seem peppy today.

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:53.090
I think Lady Luck finally remembered I was here.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:53.540
Eh?

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:57.440
Yesterday, I met this really cute girl!

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:58.050
Huh?

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.050
Here, let me tell you all the details.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.430
A first-year student from Hakuhyou Academy?

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.440
Yeah.

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.930
You can’t go wrong by looking at the uniform and the badge.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.100
She was waiting at the school gate?

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.390
Yeah. She was waiting for me!

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:16.260
I think she really likes me!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:20.060
But… she asked a lot of
questions about you.

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:21.650
About me?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:28.710
Like who are you going out with. She knows about the Ichijou sisters as well…

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:32.080
Then I think she was talking about the Chigusa sisters when she asked about

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:35.460
your relationship with the
“veterinary clinic sisters”…

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:42.510
It felt awkward when she asked me these all of a sudden, but that’s so cute.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.840
Although she seems a bit harsh, isn’t that even better?

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.260
Maybe it’s Soujyu-chan?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.340
But she’s not harsh at all.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:59.520
I really thought that was Soujyu-chan… maybe she has a twin?

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:01.360
But how could that be?

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:04.590
Hey, what are you smirking about?

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:11.950
Eh?

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:13.960
Soujyu-chan?

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:19.380
No? You’re…?

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:24.270
If you make Soujyu cry, I will never forgive you.

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:27.430
Break off all relations with the other girls, and go out with Soujyu!

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:29.180
Eh?

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:10.790 --> 00:23:11.610
This is Kira!

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:12.530
This is Yura!

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:14.500
It’s finally the cultural festival!

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:16.750
We’re cosplaying as mermaids!

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:18.830
Soujyu-chan and Sara-chan
have also come!

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:20.960
We’re happy, but…

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.800
Next time: Pastel Sunset
